WEBVTT

00:00:00.165 --> 00:00:04.525
A repeatable workflow begins with authorization, mission planning, aircraft assignment,

00:00:04.525 --> 00:00:07.560
weather and airspace review, crew briefing, equipment preparation,

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:08.865
and preflight inspection.

00:00:08.865 --> 00:00:12.320
Each step should have a clear owner and a record appropriate to the risk.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.940
At launch, establish a controlled area, confirm communications, verify aircraft status,

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:19.120
and climb only after stable control is clear.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:21.610
The team should know the initial route, first decision point,

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:24.080
and the words used to call an abort or landing.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:28.190
During flight, the pilot monitors aircraft position, link quality, battery, weather,

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:29.504
hazards, and surrounding traffic.

00:00:29.504 --> 00:00:33.960
The payload operator or observer supports mission tasks without distracting from safety.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:36.940
Record deviations and significant events as they occur.

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:39.910
Recovery is a planned phase, not the moment the battery becomes urgent.

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:42.900
Clear the landing area, announce the approach, maintain margins,

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.960
and secure the aircraft after touchdown.

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:48.440
Treat damaged or abnormal batteries according to approved safety procedures.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:52.035
Post-flight work includes inspecting the aircraft, recording maintenance concerns,

00:00:52.035 --> 00:00:55.340
accounting for batteries and media, offloading data into approved storage,

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:57.489
and completing the flight log.

00:00:57.489 --> 00:01:01.240
Do not erase or reformat original media until handling requirements are satisfied.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:04.205
An after-action review asks what happened, what worked, what changed,

00:01:04.205 --> 00:01:05.920
and what should improve.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:08.720
Update checklists, training, risk controls, and maintenance actions.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:12.640
A disciplined workflow turns each flight into evidence for safer future operations.
